Project Schedule
RAS has assigned its Executive Leadership Team to this project to ensure the successful completion of the
Roadway Network Condition update.  RAS embraces a Critical Path Method (CPM) to project scheduling
which includes building out a project roadmap to help visualize what needs to be done to reach the project
end goal. The RAS project management technique involves mapping out key milestones or critical tasks
necessary to complete a project including kickoff meeting, GIS data review, Data Collection, field pilot
validation, pavement condition assessment, final deliverables and areas involving City input to avoid
bottlenecks. RAS will work with the City in establishing key milestones as part of the CPM.
Due to the winter season approaching, data collection will be scheduled for late winter or early spring
(late March or early April) to avoid the coldest of temperatures and optimize daily field production.  The
RAC Laser Crack Measurement System has an automated cold weather shut down procedure that
generally initiates around 32 degrees Fahrenheit to protect its internal components.
The RAS team collects an excess of 30 pavement/ROW assessments annually and has an outstanding
reputation of completing projects of similar size and scale on time and within budget. Progress meetings
will be held at increments established with the City, to ensure clear expectations, facilitate open
communication, and ensure mutual understanding of the project requirements and deliverables.
